  "On a corner": "",
  "`position` puts the badge on a corner of what it is in. `Badge.attach` does it programmatically, on any component.": "",
  "Read where it stands, as part of what it is in.": "",
  "With a label the badge is an image with that name (`role=\"img\"`), so a count can say what it counts.": "",
  "Without a label a dot is hidden from screen readers (`aria-hidden`): give it one when it says something.": "",
  "The tone is never the only way something is said: pair a tone with a text or a label.": "",
  "A count is written in the kit language (`uiLocale`), again when it changes: “1,234” in English, “1.234” in Turkish.": "",
  "The badge. `data-tone`, `data-variant`, `data-size`, `data-position`, `data-dot`, `data-empty`.": "",
  "What a badge on a corner sits on (`position: relative`).": "",
  "Unit: the badge, at rest (solid, standard), in each look and tone (`accent` … `danger`, `subtle-*`, `outline-*`) and as a `dot`.": "",
  "The badge and the dot per size.": "",
  "How far a badge on a corner sits in from it.": "",
  "The tone and look a badge takes when none is given.": "",
  "A short text; shown while there is no `count`.": "",
  "A count, written in the kit language; over `max` it shows `max+`.": "",
  "The highest count written as it is.": "",
  "A count of 0 shows; without it the badge hides at 0.": "",
  "A dot only: there is something, without saying what.": "",
  "`standard`, `accent`, `info`, `success`, `caution`, `danger`. Material marks counts in `danger`, the other languages in `accent`.": "",
  "the language’s (`solid`)": "",
  "`top-end`, `top-start`, `bottom-end`, `bottom-start`: on that corner of what it is in, which becomes its anchor. `start` and `end` follow the writing direction.": "",
  "What screen readers say (“3 unread messages”); without it they read the text.": "",
  "What it shows now: the count as written (`99+`), else the text; `''` for a dot.": "",
  "Puts a badge on a corner of a component (`top-end` unless `props` says otherwise). It becomes one of its children and goes with it.": ""
